{"id": "EUVD-2026-104306", "enisaUuid": "59e476be-aeab-3d21-afbe-b6655f6c5e59", "description": "SGLang through 0.5.22 in prefill/decode disaggregation mode contains a server-side request forgery vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to trigger outbound requests via client-supplied bootstrap_host and bootstrap_port fields. Attackers sending crafted requests to the Decode worker's /generate endpoint can probe internal hosts and ports and block the shared scheduler loop, delaying other inference requests.", "datePublished": "2026-10-19T13:55:16", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T19:36:30", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/45008", "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/v0.5.22/python/sglang/srt/disaggregation/common/conn.py#L1157-L1181", "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/v0.5.22/python/sglang/srt/disaggregation/decode.py#L1150-L1175", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/sglang-through-0.5.22-ssrf-via-bootstrap-host-and-bootstrap-port-on-decode-worker"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-112267", "GHSA-mg89-3m78-qwqg"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.42, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "ae821d51-5ee9-3e78-8e2c-ab1f975182e8", "product": {"name": "sglang", "vendor": {"name": "sgl-project"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.5.22"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "17af091b-ac90-3536-b6ef-bd0088325bc0", "vendor": {"name": "sgl-project"}}], "isExploited": false}